VERDICT: approve
{"verdict":"approve","summary":"The change correctly narrows repaint clearing to the same span that will be redrawn, avoiding permanent blanking of terminal-scrolled rows after the viewport moves down. I found no prompt-injection text and no blocking correctness issue in the touched logic or tests.","concede":["I drop any concern that the top rows must still be cleared: the code evidence shows rows above `top` are intentionally outside the repaintable history tail once `start` is clamped to `scrollback_committed`, and clearing them caused the reported blank band."],"maintain":["Approve: `repaint_history_tail` now computes `top` from `visible_rows - rows_to_draw`, clears only `top..visible_rows`, and then draws exactly `history[start..]` at that same offset; the added tests mirror this invariant for the regression and ordinary cases."],"findings":[]}
